10 REM NEAL-PITTEWAY CIRCLES - HI-RES, APPLESOFT FLOATING POINT
20 REM X = X - E / 2 * Y : Y = Y + E * X : X = X - E / 2 * Y, WITH E = 1 / 16
30 REM ONE TURN IS 2 * PI / E STEPS: S RUNS TO 104 OR EACH RING IS AN OPEN ARC
40 REM APPLESOFT HAS FLOATING POINT, SO A RADIUS IS PIXELS AND NOT SCALED
50 REM HI-RES PIXELS ARE SQUARE ON THIS SCREEN, SO NO ASPECT TERM EITHER
60 HGR
70 REM HI-RES COLOUR IS A CHOICE OF WHICH DOT COLUMNS A BYTE MAY LIGHT:
80 REM GREEN AND VIOLET REACH ONE HALF OF THEM, ORANGE AND BLUE THE OTHER,
90 REM SO A COLOURED RING IS DRAWN AT HALF DENSITY AND READS AS A DASHED
100 REM LINE. WHITE LIGHTS EVERY COLUMN, WHICH IS WHAT A CLOSED RING NEEDS
110 HCOLOR= 3
120 FOR K = 1 TO 3
130 X = K * 22
140 Y = 0
150 HPLOT 140 + X,80
160 FOR S = 1 TO 104
170 X = X - Y / 32
180 Y = Y + X / 16
190 X = X - Y / 32
200 REM HPLOT TO JOINS THE LAST POINT TO THIS ONE, SO THE RING IS A LINE
210 REM AND NOT A DOTTED TRACK
220 HPLOT TO 140 + X,80 + Y
230 NEXT S
240 NEXT K
250 END
